║                                                                                 ‹  star  browser ║
║         Why the borrow checker says no: a field guide to lifetimes                               ║
║         Jane Example · example.org · 20 Sep 2026 · 1 min                                         ║
║                                                                                                  ║
║         The borrow checker is not a wall. It is a very patient reviewer that has read            █
║         the nomicon [1] and every &'a str in your crate, and would like a word [2] about         █
║         three of them.[^1]                                                                       █
║                                                                                                  ║
║                                                                                                  ║
║         Three rules                                                                              ║
║                                                                                                  ║
║         • Every value has exactly one owner.                                                     ║
║         • You may borrow it, but not while it is being changed.                                  ║
║           • A shared borrow is many.                                                             ║
║           • A mutable borrow is one.                                                             ║
║         • A borrow may not outlive what it borrows.                                              ║
║                                                                                                  ║
║         1. Name the lifetime.                                                                    ║
║         2. Make the compiler agree with the name.                                                ║
